AAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1786047143699433001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"0d702111-568a-41cd-80f9-433d8267d077","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"ad16-30a7-adb6-454a"}],"description":"Scope: `src/rebar/_store/**`, `reducer/**`, `graph/**`, `_snapshot/**`. ~230 lines leave, mostly relocations.\n\nIMPORTANT NEGATIVE RESULT — this shard establishes that comment triage CANNOT fix the two size-pressured files here, and the epic must not pretend otherwise. `_store/event_append.py` (791/800) recovers ~10 lines; `reducer/_processors.py` (777/800) recovers ~3. Their comments ARE the replay-compat justifications. The real seams were identified instead: the two `_recover_from_*` helpers in event_append (`_recover_from_unmerged`, `_recover_from_invalid_object`; ~140 lines) and `process_snapshot`'s four migration blocks in _processors (~80 lines). Those splits are OUT OF SCOPE here.\n\nVerified stale: `reducer/llm_format.py:1-28` documents a key map that omits four keys present in `KEY_MAP` directly below it AND cites a module path that does not exist; `_store/gitutil.py:3-4` claims it 'imports nothing from rebar.*' while :214 imports from `rebar._commands.fsck`; `_store/hlc.py:35-36` says a kill-switch reverts 'for one release' — four schema bumps ago — over a still-wired, still-tested code path; `reducer/_filters.py:1-11` justifies itself by a bash/Python duality that no longer exists.\n\n`reducer/_version.py:39-66` duplicates the wire-format changelog that `docs/event-schema.md` also holds in a PARTIAL, STALE copy (has v2/v3, missing v4/v5). Two homes, one drifting.\n\nCheapest win in the whole audit: `graph/_graph.py:250-254` states the same sentence twice, once as a noqa suffix and once as the block below it.\n\nThe do_not_move list here is the most important of the six: 21 entries, with `reducer/_processors.py:719-774` flagged as highest-risk — four SNAPSHOT-restore migration guards where relocating the rationale makes live guards look like dead defensive code, one of which explicitly warns the guard must NOT run unconditionally because the else-branch would clobber a recorded channel with 'unknown'.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Every non-KEEP unit in scope is relocated or deleted per its destination\n- [ ] The shard's do_not_move list is appended to `.joe-janitor/tools.md` BEFORE any edit lands\n- [ ] Verified-stale comments are corrected where they document a live invariant, deleted only where obsolete\n- [ ] No load-bearing invariant is lost\n## CORRECTION (plan-review preempt, parent 373f disposition vocabulary)\n\nSuperseding ACs below encode the 373f disposition rules, the verified-stale corrections (each\nconfirmed against the code), the two-homes changelog consolidation (info must be ADDED to the\ncanonical home before the duplicate is collapsed), and the highest-risk do_not_move set (the\nsnapshot-restore migration guards). This shard's NEGATIVE RESULT stands: the two size-pressured\nfiles are NOT fixed by comment triage.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria (supersedes the list above)\n\n- [ ] Every substantial in-scope comment unit is dispositioned into exactly one parent-373f\n      label: RELOCATE (to docs, reduced to a one-line citation), DELETE, KEEP, DO_NOT_MOVE, or\n      CORRECT-IN-PLACE.\n- [ ] Decision rule CORRECT-vs-DELETE: a comment documenting CURRENT runtime behavior / a live\n      invariant is CORRECTED in place; DELETE only when its referent no longer exists. Every\n      DELETE records its reason (referenced-artifact-gone / superseded) in the commit body.\n- [ ] These verified-stale comments are CORRECTED in place (referent still LIVE):\n      `_store/gitutil.py:3-4` (\"imports nothing from rebar.*\" is false — line ~214 has a\n      FUNCTION-LOCAL `from rebar._commands.fsck import _resolve_tracker_git_dir`; correct to\n      \"no MODULE-LEVEL rebar imports; one deferred in-function import\"); `reducer/llm_format.py:1-28`\n      (the docstring's Key-mapping block must enumerate the FOUR live maps — KEY_MAP,\n      COMMENT_KEY_MAP, DEP_KEY_MAP, INBOUND_KEY_MAP — and its FIRST line cites the STALE package\n      path `ticket_reducer/llm_format.py`; the module now lives at `reducer/llm_format.py` (the\n      package was renamed `ticket_reducer`->`reducer`). CORRECT that header path to\n      `reducer/llm_format.py` (or drop the bare-path line) and make the enumeration match the four\n      live maps' key sets); `_store/hlc.py:35-36` (\"reverts ... for one release\"\n      is stale by four schema bumps over a still-wired, still-tested REBAR_HLC=0 path; correct the\n      \"one release\" phrasing, KEEP the kill-switch description).\n- [ ] `reducer/_filters.py:1-11` justifies itself by a bash/Python duality that no longer exists:\n      RELOCATE any still-true content and DELETE the obsolete duality justification (reason:\n      referenced-artifact-gone — the bash side is gone).\n- [ ] Two-homes changelog consolidation (NO information loss): `reducer/_version.py:39-66` and\n      `docs/event-schema.md` both hold the wire-format changelog; docs is PARTIAL/STALE (has\n      v2/v3, missing v4/v5). FIRST bring `docs/event-schema.md` to the COMPLETE set (add the v4\n      and v5 entries from `_version.py`), THEN collapse the `_version.py` prose changelog to a\n      one-line \"see docs/event-schema.md\" citation. The canonical home must be complete before\n      the code copy is reduced. Observable oracle:\n      `grep -q 'v4' docs/event-schema.md && grep -q 'v5' docs/event-schema.md` passes AND the\n      `_version.py` changelog comment block (~39-66) collapses to a single citation line\n      (`grep -c '^# v[2-5]' src/rebar/reducer/_version.py` returns 0 afterward).\n- [ ] `graph/_graph.py:250-254` states the same sentence twice (a `# noqa: BLE001` suffix AND the\n      block comment below it): KEEP the `# noqa` pragma line intact (DO_NOT_MOVE), DELETE the\n      redundant block comment that restates it (reason: superseded — duplicate of the pragma\n      rationale).\n- [ ] NEGATIVE RESULT preserved: `_store/event_append.py` (791/800) and `reducer/_processors.py`\n      (777/800) are NOT size-fixed by comment triage — their comments are replay-compat\n      justifications. Recover only the trivially-recoverable lines (~10 / ~3); DO NOT strip\n      load-bearing replay-compat rationale to chase headroom. The real splits (the four\n      `_recover_from_*` helpers — `_recover_from_unmerged` and `_recover_from_invalid_object`; and `process_snapshot`'s SNAPSHOT-restore migration guards) are OUT OF SCOPE.\n- [ ] HIGHEST-RISK do_not_move (verbatim): `reducer/_processors.py:719-774` — the four\n      SNAPSHOT-restore migration guards. Relocating their rationale would make live guards look\n      like dead defensive code; one guard's comment explicitly warns it must NOT run\n      unconditionally (the else-branch would clobber a recorded channel with 'unknown'). These\n      stay verbatim.\n- [ ] A `## da4c` section is appended to `.joe-janitor/tools.md` BEFORE any edit lands, and it\n      records EACH comment unit dispositioned DO_NOT_MOVE/KEEP as one `path:line — reason` row\n      (the count is whatever the triage yields — an OUTPUT, not a target). Observable oracle: the\n      section MUST contain, at minimum, a row for `reducer/_processors.py:719-774` (the four\n      snapshot-restore guards) — verify with\n      `grep -A40 '## da4c' .joe-janitor/tools.md | grep -q '_processors.py:719-774'`. Lint/type\n      pragmas and test-introspected docstrings encountered in scope are recorded as DO_NOT_MOVE.\n- [ ] The actual recovered comment-line count is measured (by diff) and recorded on this ticket\n      as an OUTPUT, not a target.\n- [ ] No behaviour change: the full test suite AND `make lint` / `make typecheck` pass unchanged.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py","reason":"Correct module docstring: it has two deferred function-local rebar imports, not zero"},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/hlc.py","reason":"Correct the stale for-one-release horizon on the REBAR_HLC=0 kill-switch (path still live)"},{"path":"src/rebar/reducer/llm_format.py","reason":"Correct docstring to enumerate all four key maps and fix the non-existent module path it cites"},{"path":"src/rebar/reducer/_filters.py","reason":"Delete the obsolete bash/Python-duality justification (bash side gone); relocate any still-true content"},{"path":"src/rebar/reducer/_version.py","reason":"Collapse the v2-v5 changelog to a docs citation AFTER the docs are completed"},{"path":"src/rebar/graph/_graph.py","reason":"Delete the block comment that duplicates the noqa BLE001 pragma rationale (keep the pragma)"},{"path":"docs/event-schema.md","reason":"Add the missing v4 and v5 wire-format changelog rows so docs is authoritative before the code copy collapses"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"4d084713-8164-4b68-9afe-601bbda46966","managed_refs":[["depends_on","ad16-30a7-adb6-454a"],["parent","373f-8c1d-cef0-41bf"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"373f-8c1d-cef0-41bf","parent_status_uuid":"8f0e614c-c220-4fda-b86d-effa39ca4eef","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["janitor"],"ticket_id":"da4c-30d0-0cc5-4254","ticket_type":"task","title":"Comment triage: store, reducer, graph and snapshot","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["db5b9fc2-d7ba-4b88-9a0c-1a0574d1177b","0d702111-568a-41cd-80f9-433d8267d077","4c864470-62f8-4cf6-aac4-c67d6d6623fa","617753c0-a118-485e-8207-a9d040f0c1db","cce04ab3-af42-4a77-aea1-89200bd1c802","8bcad250-f053-46b0-8229-136ae911a5ea","b7420c56-356a-47b7-9044-e0103c313fc4","d79831d8-f4bc-4ff8-ade2-5d72880f98a2","8f0e61